      "summary": "The added HTTP scenarios exercise reset outcomes through the endpoint, but they do not catch an implementation that excludes denied-role requests from quota when they arrive below the limit.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/CasePackRequestLimiterTests.cs",
          "line": 221,
          "message": "AC-030's endpoint test does not prove that a denied-role attempt consumes quota. Follow a denied-role response received below the limit with enough authenticated attempts to verify that it used one of the three slots.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "AC030_ResetAttemptsCountEveryAuthenticatedOutcome sends endpoint requests with presenter and non-presenter roles. The first scenario checks a denied-role response but makes no later request to check whether it consumed quota; in another scenario, the denied-role request arrives after three attempts and is rate-limited before role handling.",
            "failureScenario": "If the endpoint skips recording quota for denied-role requests while under the limit, the test still passes: the early denied-role case ends at 403, and the later one is already blocked at the limit. The test therefore does not prove AC-030's requirement that a denied-role attempt consumes quota."
          }
        }
      ]
